From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meta-microos <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 1970 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Do not hand the native rpm's config path to a scriptlet

poky's dnf wrapper exports RPM_CONFIGDIR and RPM_ETCCONFIGDIR so that the
relocatable rpm-native can find its own macros in the recipe sysroot. rpm
passes its whole environment to a scriptlet, and upstream rpm reads both
variables (rpmio/rpmfileutil.c, lib/rpmrc.c).

In meta-microos the scriptlet runs inside a real chroot into the image, so
those two paths do not exist there. Any scriptlet that calls the image's own
rpm therefore fails:

  /usr/bin/permctl -n --set --system /usr/bin/su
  error: Unable to open .../recipe-sysroot-native/usr/lib/rpm/rpmrc for reading
  /usr/bin/su: rpm sub-process exited with 1. Cannot determine package ownership.

Drop both variables in the scriptlet child, next to where rpm sets PATH. The
image's rpm then uses its own compiled-in /usr/lib/rpm, and the parent process
keeps the variables it needs.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [meta-microos specific]
---
 lib/rpmscript.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/lib/rpmscript.c
+++ b/lib/rpmscript.c
@@ -256,6 +256,10 @@
 	free(ipath);
     }
 
+    /* The scriptlet runs inside the image, where the native rpm is not. */
+    unsetenv("RPM_CONFIGDIR");
+    unsetenv("RPM_ETCCONFIGDIR");
+
     for (ARGV_const_t pf = prefixes; pf && *pf; pf++) {
 	char *name = NULL;
 	int num = (pf - prefixes);
